## Tier 1: Screening — Detailed Design

### Model Selection Rationale

| Model | F1 on Chinese MH Data | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Chinese MentalBERT | 88.39% | Domain-specific pre-training on Chinese mental health social media |
| Chinese BERT (general) | ~72% | No domain adaptation |
| Multilingual BERT | ~68% | English-dominant; non-Latin script gap (DeepMind, 2025) |
| GPT-4 (prompted) | ~74% | Fails on indirect Chinese distress expression |

### Cultural Adaptation Notes

Asian adolescents express distress differently from Western populations:

- **Academic pressure framing:** "我考試又不及格了" (Failed exam again) — may indicate deeper distress
- **Somatic language:** "我頭很痛，睡不著" (Headache, can't sleep) — physical complaints often mask psychological distress
- **Indirect expression:** "最近好累" (So tired lately) — exhaustion as distress proxy
- **Family pressure markers:** References to parental expectations, shame, filial obligation
- **Code-switching:** Mixed Mandarin/English common in Singapore — "好stressed, cannot tahan anymore"

