## Tier 2: Risk Scoring — Detailed Design

### Feature Engineering

**Linguistic Features:**
- Hopelessness score — future-negative language frequency
- Negation density — "cannot", "never", "no point" patterns
- Help-seeking signals — explicit and implicit support requests
- Emotional valence trajectory — sentiment change over time

**Temporal Features:**
- Late-night posting frequency (11pm–4am)
- Posting frequency change — sudden increase or decrease
- Recency weighting — recent signals weighted more heavily

**Cultural Context Features (Asian adolescent-specific):**
- Academic stress markers — exam period, results, rankings
- Family pressure language — parental expectations, shame
- Social comparison — "everyone is better than me"
- Face-saving language — indirect distress through performance framing

